# Every text file is checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# This is not tidiness. A mod's compatibility digest is taken over its entry's
# text and its tuning tree (see `crates/mods`), so a `\r\n` checkout of the same
# commit on Windows and an `\n` one on Linux produced different hashes for the
# same mod, and the two ends refused each other's sessions -- and the `birds.zip`
# in the Windows and Linux release archives differed for the same reason. With
# `eol=lf` a checkout is the same bytes everywhere, so a session and a release do
# not depend on who built them.
#
# The loader normalises line endings when it reads a mod's text, so a mod that
# was zipped on Windows still joins a Linux host; this is what keeps the checked-in
# fixtures themselves reproducible.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries are left exactly as they are: `text=auto` would usually detect them,
# but the ones this repository carries are worth naming so a future heuristic
# change cannot start rewriting a model or a sound.
*.blend binary
*.blend1 binary
*.fbx binary
*.glb binary
*.mp4 binary
*.ogg binary
*.png binary
*.wav binary
*.wasm binary
*.zip binary
